                    insight_led:            `You led the turn: engagement, transformation progress and stakeholder trust all rising together. You treated purpose, people and stakeholders as one integrated act — and the anchor sees a transformation it can renew against, run by a workforce that believes in it.`,
                    insight_brokepeople:    `You hit the numbers but broke the people. Progress and trust are credible, yet engagement collapsed or the loyalty asset was cut away. White's evidence is unforgiving here — a transformation the workforce doesn't believe in decays the moment the pressure that forced it eases.`,
                    insight_lostmarket:     `You kept the people but lost the market window. Engagement held, but transformation progress and stakeholder trust never reached a credible trajectory — and the anchor, seeing no visible proof before month 11, has little reason to renew.`,
                    insight_stalled:        `The turn stalled. Neither the human nor the commercial side reached a credible position. Re-examine which classic error you fell into — technology-first, the burning platform, speed over capacity, the over-promised win, or one message for all.`,
                    insight_strike:         `The compulsory cuts triggered union action that depressed engagement and progress for the rest of the turn. You bought four months of speed and lost the 11-year tenure loyalty that was your only capacity to execute.`,
                    insight_anchorlost:     `Without visible progress and credible trust before month 11, the anchor client walked — and on the concept's escalation logic, the grocer is expected to follow, putting 46% of revenue and the AIM listing in play.`,
                    insight_overpromised:   `You pledged a client-visible win you could not deliver, and when it slipped you spent credibility you needed at the trough. Momentum has to be engineered to be deliverable — a smaller promise over-delivered beats a big one missed.`,
                    insight_lowengagement:  `Engagement finished below where it started. The human-centered constraint was treated as a slogan, not a boundary — and a disengaged workforce cannot run the very automation the transformation depends on.`,
                    insight_lasts:          `This is a turn that lasts: the people are with you, the progress is real, and the stakeholders believe it. Six months on, the transformation is still moving — because you led people through it, not around them.`,

                    hint_strike:            `A strike is suppressing engagement and progress every round. Compulsory cuts destroyed the loyalty asset — there is no fast way back, but honest, consistent leadership at the trough can limit the bleed.`,
                    hint_overpromise:       `You've made a bold client pledge. The trough is coming — make sure your Round 4 response fronts the slip honestly, or the over-promise will cost you the trust you'll need most.`,
                    hint_engagement:        `Engagement is dangerously low — the human-centered constraint is being treated as a slogan. Lead with purpose, protect the floor's capacity, and stop transforming faster than people can absorb.`,
